sition": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "electropop": {"genre": "electropop", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "Electropop is a type of electronic pop music which features crackly synthesizers prominently in the mix.   Electropop has become an increasingly common term for this music post-2000 whereas in earlier years, synthpop was probably the more common term for pop music using synthesizers.\n\nWhen Kraftwerk first appeared in the mid-1970's, their music was described as electronic body music (ebm) in Germany, Krautrock in England, and technopop in Japan.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chase Atlantic", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Dua Lipa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Katy Perry", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Maroon 5", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rihanna", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sabrina Carpenter", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Taylor Swift", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "hip-hop": {"genre": "hip-hop", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "Hip-Hop, also spelled Hip Hop or HipHop is a rhythm focused popular music style, originating from New York in The 70s. The term rap is sometimes used synonymously with Hip-Hop music. Hip-hop arose when DJs began isolating the percussion break from funk or disco songs for audiences to dance to.\nIt is now seen as a worldwide and popular genre ranging from American Mainstream (e.g. Eminem, Lil Wayne) to British Underground (e.g. Wiley, EMC Junkie ect).", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Karan Aujla", "streams": 1127885, "best_position": 24}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Childish Gambino", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Djo", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Don Toliver", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Eminem", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Frank Ocean", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Future", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Gorillaz", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "J. Cole", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "jazz": {"genre": "jazz", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "Jazz is a musical art form which originated around the beginning of the 20th century in Black communities in the Southern United States from a confluence of African and European music traditions. The style's West African pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Steve Lacy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "BTS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jung Kook", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Sai Abhyankkar", "streams": 2081180, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Anuv Jain", "streams": 1668013, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "Arijit Singh", "streams": 1465638, "best_position": 30}, {"artist": "Anirudh Ravichander", "streams": 1269314, "best_position": 40}, {"artist": "A$AP Rocky", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Amit Trivedi", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charli xcx", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "psychedelic rock": {"genre": "psychedelic rock", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "Psychedelic rock is a subgenre of rock that emerged in the '60s. It is influenced by the psychedelic culture of the time, and psychedelic (psychotropic) drugs, such as LSD and shrooms.\n\nThe musical style often incorporates flowing, hypnotic rhythms. Typical instruments associated with the genre include electric guitar, which is often augmented with effects pedals; various types of organs, which include Hammonds and Farfisas; bass guitar, and drums. Vocals in psychedelic rock music are also sometimes augmented with effects.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Maroon 5", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Pink Floyd", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Tame Impala", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Beatles", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "in", "country_name": "India", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Charlie Puth", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Chase Atlantic", "streams": null, "b